Three candidate palettes, in the three formats the tool reads, so that
`palette_curate.py` has something to run on out of the box and each parser is
documented by example:

    benten-pond.hex    one hex code per line       (Lospec .hex export)
    dungeon-20.json    {name, author, colors[]}    (Lospec's JSON endpoint)
    oekakinl.gpl       GIMP palette                (GIMP, Aseprite, Krita)

    uv run tools/palette_curate.py score tools/candidates-example/
    uv run tools/palette_curate.py sheet tools/candidates-example/ -o sheet.html

These particular three are the palettes the fork already adopted at indices
15-17, which makes them a useful regression check rather than a neutral sample:
the fitter's output can be read against the hand-curated mapping in
`tools/palette_analysis.py` to see where a human overrode the algorithm, and
why. They are NOT the tool's recommendations - see doc/palette-curation.md for
what the fitter gets wrong on each.

A .pal (JASC-PAL) file works too; there simply is not one here.

Credits, as in doc/palette-set.md:
